   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the state technology law, in relation to the use of biometric\nidentifying technology; and to repeal certain provisions of the education law\nrelating thereto",
    "basePrintNo": "S893",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S893-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2-e, Ed L (as proposed in S.5140-B & A.6787-D); add §106-b, St Tech L",
    "lawSection": "State Technology Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S893\n\nSPONSOR: KAVANAGH\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the state technology law, in relation to the use of\nbiometric identifying technology; and to repeal certain provisions of\nthe education law relating thereto\n\n \nPURPOSE OF BILL:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of L.2020,\nc.349.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by adding language to\nprovide exceptions to the prohibition on biometric identifying technolo-\ngy in schools, and shifts oversight of the study to the Office of Infor-\nmation Technology Services.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPursuant to approval memo 53 of 2020, the Executive expressed concern\nwith unintended consequences of the underlying legislation, while\nsupporting its goals. This legislation is a negotiated change to the\nunderlying chapter that addresses those concerns.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 349 of the Laws of 2020.   \nFISCAL IMPLI-\nCATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
